<cem:title lang="" subtitle="">PRONUNCIATION SPOT Looking at Both Sides</cem:title>
<cem:description lang="">This virtual learning object "PRONUNCIATION SPOT Looking at Both Sides" that makes part of the lesson No: 18, Big Decisions, which in turn belongs to the Intermediate (B1.3) of the teaching of English as a Foreign Language, is intended to work on: explain your opinions. Also, the vocabulary considers: decision making, e.g., to make up your mind, to reflect on. Finally, the pronunciation in this LO is linking words with the same consonant sound, e.g., they are right here; silent syllables with unstressed vowels, e.g., vegetable, chocolate, diamond.</cem:description>
<cem:keyword lang="">
<cem:li>Words with the same sound</cem:li>
<cem:li>Silent syllables</cem:li>
</cem:keyword>
