<cem:description>
<cem:recommendedUse lang="en">This digital resource can be used as an activity that allows the learner to reflect on the use of grammar of English language in different communicative contexts. The instructor can work further on activities and tasks that help learners to improve their procedural knowledge.</cem:recommendedUse>
<cem:triggerQuestion lang="en">What is the hardest decision you ever had to make? How did you make your decision?; Do you have a strategy or method for making important decisions? What is it?</cem:triggerQuestion>
<cem:pedagogicalAspect lang="en">This learning object "PRONUNCIATION SPOT Looking at Both Sides" that is part of the lesson No: 18, Big Decisions, which in turn belongs to the Intermediate (B1.3). It is presented within the context of explain your opinions. The student will be exposed to vocabulary related to: decision making, e.g., to make up your mind, to reflect on. Finally, the pronunciation in this LO is: linking words with the same consonant sound, e.g., they are right here; silent syllables with unstressed vowels, e.g., vegetable, chocolate, diamond. Learners will develop their language skills by using an online content as well as the guidance of a SENA instructor.</cem:pedagogicalAspect>
<cem:learningGoal lang="en">The purpose of this learning object is to accurately use information about people’s backgrounds in a wider variety of communicative situations.</cem:learningGoal>
</cem:description>
</cem:educational>
